```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the `cur_msg_mapped` flag is set to `true` even when there are no valid transfers mapped in the SPI message. The loop iterating over `msg->transfers` may not execute if there are no transfers, leading to the flag being incorrectly set. This can result in the code mistakenly treating the message as DMA mapped, which can cause it to invoke DMA-related APIs on unmapped data, leading to undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = -ENOMSG;
```
```c
if (ret)
    return 0;
```
Reason:
The fix introduces an early return mechanism that checks if any transfers were successfully mapped. By initializing `ret` to `-ENOMSG` and checking its value after the transfer mapping loop, the code can determine if no transfers were mapped. If no transfers are present, it prevents the `cur_msg_mapped` flag from being set to `true`, thus avoiding the incorrect invocation of DMA-related APIs on unmapped data.

